| AC-02 | APPROVED | E-CONTRACTS: seven behavioral tests | Linux/Python observed environment; no product approval |
| AC-03 | APPROVED | E-CLOSURE: 63 fast + 20 integration tests, check-ox, maintenance and semantic review | Affected predecessor feature criteria remain INCONCLUSIVE; graphical acceptance outside scope |

Current report and raw final/intermediate logs: docs/validation/scripts-task-closure/report.md.
No mandatory criterion of this governance feature remains UNVERIFIED. The two
invalidation manifests enumerate affected historical criteria requiring successor
review, preserving their prior observations and unrelated operational evidence.

## Security/quality successor

The maintainer clarified that applicable Rust/Python/security capabilities must
remain. The deletion rationale above is historical and superseded for those files
by scripts-security-quality. Its inventory is the current disposition. The three
predecessor criteria are now INCONCLUSIVE on changed inputs, with exact prior
observations/preimages preserved; they are not current approval of the corrected
contract. See the successor feature and docs/decisions/scripts-security-quality.md.

